meta {
  name: Retrieve Sample
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/retrieve
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "notes": "Sent to the wrong branch"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200); });
}

docs {
  Universal undo. For an internal transfer the sender can retrieve the sample only
  while the transfer is IN_TRANSIT or PICKED_UP: the transfer is recalled (REJECTED,
  reason "Recalled via Retrieve") and the sample returns to ACCEPTED.

  Refused (422 SAMPLE_RETRIEVE_BLOCKED) once the receiving branch has received or
  accepted it, and for a sample that already came back from the receiving branch
  (status REPEAT with previous status SENT_INTERNAL) - collect it again instead.
  Any other action on a SENT_INTERNAL sample (repeat, store, return, send... even
  with `force`) is refused with 422 SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH.
  Internal branch transfer rules (manager flow 2026-09-29):
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER's Technician
    worklist hides its report (list, counts, detail, history, every write, the five
    secondary worklists, attachments, inventory usage, analyser results). It behaves
    as "Lab report not found" (404 LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND) for the sender.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.
}
